---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
import OneSlideDeck from '@layouts/OneSlideDeck.astro';

const title = "Building Globally Relevant AI & Deeptech Companies";
const description = "Kauffman Summit perspectives on AI-native and deeptech startups, with Parslee-focused follow-up meetings";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <OneSlideDeck>
      <section class="title-slide">
        <h1>Building Globally Relevant AI & Deeptech Companies</h1>
        <h2>Kauffman Fellows Summit Perspectives</h2>
        <p><em>Parslee-focused follow-ups and market insights</em></p>
        <div class="author-info">
          <p>Michael Staton | 2025</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Context: Kauffman Fellows Summit</h2>
        <ul>
          <li class="fragment">Global network of venture investors and deeptech builders</li>
          <li class="fragment">Workshop day hosted by Notion VC, Playfair Capital, and Dawn Capital</li>
          <li class="fragment">Focus on AI-native, deeptech, and globally scalable companies</li>
          <li class="fragment">Ideal environment for Parslee to deepen relationships and sharpen narrative</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <section>
          <h2>Parslee: Why This Summit Matters</h2>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">AI-native vertical product with heavy workflow and decision-support surface area</li>
            <li class="fragment">Needs early, high-signal customers who can co-develop the product</li>
            <li class="fragment">Benefits from investors who understand AI-specific metrics, not just classic SaaS</li>
            <li class="fragment">This summit concentrates exactly those companies and VCs</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>From Talk Themes to Parslee Strategy</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Defensibility will hinge on depth of customer understanding</li>
            <li class="fragment">Patience in incubation can unlock faster exponential growth later</li>
            <li class="fragment">Brand and narrative can matter as much as technical differentiation</li>
            <li class="fragment">Parslee can position itself as a "situational awareness" layer for customers</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section>
        <section>
          <h2>Proposed Parslee Meetings</h2>
          <h3>Two Buckets of Conversations</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Companies that could directly use Parslee</li>
            <li class="fragment">VCs open to strategy and product discussions</li>
            <li class="fragment">Each meeting should have a concrete learning objective</li>
            <li class="fragment">Treat these as design-partner and narrative-calibration sessions</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>Meeting Design Principles</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Aim for specific workflows, not generic demos</li>
            <li class="fragment">Bring one strong hypothesis per meeting about Parslee's value</li>
            <li class="fragment">Leave with one sharpened success metric or buying signal</li>
            <li class="fragment">Capture structured notes to refine Parslee messaging</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section>
        <section>
          <h2>Companies That Could Use Parslee</h2>
          <h3>1. Blinka</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Commercial real estate deal and loan automation platform</li>
            <li class="fragment">High-volume, high-stakes decisions on imperfect information</li>
            <li class="fragment">Parslee can support structured decision workflows and approvals</li>
            <li class="fragment">Backlink: vertical AI workspace with complex, recurring decisions</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>2. Fernstone</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Insurance policy automation for business customers</li>
            <li class="fragment">Intense regulatory and risk-compliance context</li>
            <li class="fragment">Parslee can help teams reason about edge cases and policy changes</li>
            <li class="fragment">Backlink: AI-native underwriting and policy design workflows</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>3. Michael Block (Agent Smyth background)</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Deep experience in AI-native fintech and agentic workflows</li>
            <li class="fragment">Useful mirror for Parslee's product thesis and GTM narrative</li>
            <li class="fragment">Conversation focus: "What would make Parslee indispensable to a founder like you?"</li>
            <li class="fragment">Backlink: vertical wrapper founders assessing tooling like Parslee</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section>
        <section>
          <h2>VCs Open to Parslee Conversations</h2>
          <h3>Clint Korver – Ulu Ventures</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Quantitative, decision-science background</li>
            <li class="fragment">Interest in structured decision frameworks and graduation rates</li>
            <li class="fragment">Parslee fit: "decision quality" for founders and boards</li>
            <li class="fragment">Objective: co-shape metrics that matter for AI-native workflows</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>Sherman Williams – AIN Ventures</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Sharp views on AI pilots, customer paralysis, and valuation dynamics</li>
            <li class="fragment">Concerned with traction quality and realistic paths to scale</li>
            <li class="fragment">Parslee fit: tool to separate real pull from noisy pilot signals</li>
            <li class="fragment">Objective: stress-test Parslee's value in boardroom-level decisions</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section>
        <section>
          <h2>More VC Conversations</h2>
          <h3>Mehreen Malik – MeiLin Capital</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Global growth and deeptech orientation</li>
            <li class="fragment">Likely to value disciplined, globally relevant AI narratives</li>
            <li class="fragment">Parslee fit: cross-market decision support for expansion and capital allocation</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>Ben Parr – TheoryForge</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Brand- and distribution-aware investor</li>
            <li class="fragment">Strong pattern recognition around narrative and go-to-market</li>
            <li class="fragment">Parslee fit: how to express "situational awareness" as a brand promise</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>Itxaso del Palacio – Notion VC</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Strong views on product-led growth and knowing the user deeply</li>
            <li class="fragment">Co-led round-table on customer understanding and preferences</li>
            <li class="fragment">Parslee fit: tooling for PLG companies to remember and act on customer preferences</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section>
        <section>
          <h2>Talk Theme: Success Looks Different</h2>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Standard SaaS metrics can be a distraction for AI-native teams</li>
            <li class="fragment">Founders must define their own, context-appropriate KPIs</li>
            <li class="fragment">Investors need literacy in AI-specific success patterns</li>
            <li class="fragment">Parslee can encode these custom metrics into decision workflows</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>Parslee: Candidate Success Metrics</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Time-to-high-confidence decision for complex workflows</li>
            <li class="fragment">Reduction in re-opened decisions or disputed calls</li>
            <li class="fragment">Adoption across cross-functional stakeholders in a company</li>
            <li class="fragment">Number of "situations" where Parslee becomes the canonical record</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section>
        <section>
          <h2>Defensibility: Understanding the Customer</h2>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Deep, structured customer understanding as the moat</li>
            <li class="fragment">From ad hoc notes to systematized decision histories</li>
            <li class="fragment">A Parslee instance can become an organization's memory for key calls</li>
            <li class="fragment">Backlink: Collibra-style data governance, but for decisions and context</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>Meeting Prompts for Customer Understanding</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">"Tell me about the last high-stakes decision your team made and how it went."</li>
            <li class="fragment">"Where did you feel blind or under-informed in that process?"</li>
            <li class="fragment">"Who needed to be convinced, and how did you capture their input?"</li>
            <li class="fragment">"How would you know if a tool like Parslee was really working for you?"</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section>
        <section>
          <h2>Market Dynamics & Capital</h2>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Dense competition for growth capital and attention</li>
            <li class="fragment">Down rounds and consolidation expected for many AI companies</li>
            <li class="fragment">Strategics watching research, incumbents AI-washing aggressively</li>
            <li class="fragment">Parslee can shine by clarifying which opportunities to pursue or decline</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>Using Parslee on Parslee</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Run Parslee internally on fundraising, hiring, and product bets</li>
            <li class="fragment">Use this deck and summit meetings as early Parslee case studies</li>
            <li class="fragment">Show investors the actual decision traces, not just outcomes</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Execution Plan for Parslee</h2>
        <ul>
          <li class="fragment">Prioritize the proposed meetings and schedule during the summit window</li>
          <li class="fragment">Define a clear objective and "one critical question" for each meeting</li>
          <li class="fragment">Capture structured notes into Parslee and refine success metrics</li>
          <li class="fragment">Follow up with tailored narratives for companies and VCs</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Summit as Inflection Point</h2>
        <p>Building globally relevant AI and deeptech companies requires:</p>
        <ul>
          <li class="fragment">Deeper customer understanding than competitors</li>
          <li class="fragment">Patience in incubation and clarity in focus</li>
          <li class="fragment">Narratives and brands that match the ambition of the product</li>
          <li class="fragment">Tools like Parslee that institutionalize better decisions</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="fragment" style="margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06); border-radius: 8px;">
          <p><em>Use this summit to design Parslee's next 12 months of learning and momentum.</em></p>
        </div>
      </section>

  </OneSlideDeck>
</Layout>
